<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guanqiu Jian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 255</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guanqiu Jian was a general of the Chinese state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>. In 244-245 he invaded Goguryeo, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dongcheon-of-goguryeo">King Dongcheon</a> and sacked the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hwando">Hwando</a>, pursuing the king into the Okjeo country. In 255 he rebelled against the Sima family, who controlled the Wei court, and was defeated and killed.</p></div>
